<title>USA: ITT adds 28 new hotels in 10 countries.</title>
<headline>ITT adds 28 new hotels in 10 countries.</headline>
<dateline>BOSTON 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>ITT Sheraton, a unit of ITT Corp, said Thursday it was adding 28 new hotels with over 7,000 rooms in 10 countries.</p>
<p>The new hotels include 18 Four Points hotels in the United States, Canada, and Israel, and 10 Sheraton hotels and resorts in Argentina, Canada, China, Finland, Israel, Malaysia, Mexico, the Philippines, and Vietnam.  </p>
<p>The new deals include recently completed management contracts and franchise agreements for 27 hotels and the acquisition of a hotel in Monterrey, Mexico, for a $15 million equity investment.</p>
<p>ITT Sheraton said that the transactions are immediately accretive and will generate significant cash flow over the next 10 years.</p>
<p>Daniel P. Weadock, president and chief executive officer, of ITT Sheraton, said that the company  will continue to make smart acquisitions and sign management contracts and franchise agreements.</p>
</text>
